| !Run for !Julius - RISC OS port of Julius, the open-source Caesar III
| Built with GCCSDK GCC 10.2 (arm-riscos-gnueabihf), statically linked with
| riscos-mesa's SDL2 and converted to an Absolute (AIF) file, so
| !SharedLibs isn't needed.

Set Julius$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <Julius$Dir>.!Sprites

| --- Game data --------------------------------------------------------
| Julius needs the files of the original Caesar III (CD, GOG or Steam,
| version 1.0.1.0). Copy them into C3data inside this application (see
| C3data.ReadMe), or put them anywhere and *Set Julius$Data to that
| directory (e.g. in your !Boot). Saved games and settings go there too.
If "<Julius$Data>"="" Then Set Julius$Data <Julius$Dir>.C3data

| --- Threads ----------------------------------------------------------
| SDL plays sound on a thread (UnixLib). PThreadTicker keeps it running
| while the game waits for the desktop. Loaded from !System if there,
| else ours.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 IfThere System:Modules.PThrTicker Then RMLoad System:Modules.PThrTicker
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 RMLoad <Julius$Dir>.PThrTicker

| --- Sound ------------------------------------------------------------
| Sound goes through SharedSoundBuffer, StreamManager and SharedSound
| (in !System), mixed with other programs' sound. SharedSound is part of
| RISC OS; SharedSoundBuffer and StreamManager are in ssb.zip from
| https://orac.co.uk/software/rdpclient/rdpclient.html. Without them the
| game plays silently.
RMEnsure SharedSound 1.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSound Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSound
RMEnsure StreamManager 0.03 IfThere System:Modules.StreamMan Then RMLoad System:Modules.StreamMan
RMEnsure SharedSoundBuffer 0.07 IfThere System:Modules.SSBuffer Then RMLoad System:Modules.SSBuffer

| --- Speed ------------------------------------------------------------
| The game draws at most 50 frames a second and gives the rest of the
| time back to the desktop. 0 = no limit (uses all the processor time).
| Set Julius$FPS 30

| --- Smooth scaling (try it) ------------------------------------------
| On a Pi the display hardware can scale the game's picture up smoothly
| (riscos-mesa's overlay). Set the display scale to 100% in Julius's
| options, then remove the | from both Set lines below and choose the
| size the game draws at: 1280x800 on a 1920x1200 screen looks like 150%,
| but smooth. *Show EGL$OverlayStatus afterwards says if the overlay was
| used; without it the picture is stretched by the sprite plot instead.
Unset Julius$RenderSize
Unset Julius$Overlay
| Set Julius$RenderSize 1280x800
| Set Julius$Overlay 1

| --- Logging ----------------------------------------------------------
| Normally nothing is logged. For a log in <Wimp$ScrapDir>.juliuslog
| (useful when reporting a problem), remove the | from the next line.
| Set Julius$LogOn 1
Unset Julius$Log
If "<Julius$LogOn>"<>"" Then Set Julius$Log /|<Wimp$ScrapDir>/juliuslog
Unset Julius$LogOn

| --- Memory -----------------------------------------------------------
| The C heap goes in a dynamic area ("Julius Heap", about 60 MB), so the
| WimpSlot only holds the program and its stack.
WimpSlot -min 20000K -max 20000K

Do Run <Julius$Dir>.julius %*0
